eep, dry powder:** cold Siberian air crossing the Sea of Japan buries Mt Kenashi in **8–10+ m** of snow a season, with a mid-season summit base often 4–5 m deep — among Japan''s snowiest resorts despite a modest top elevation.","source":"https://www.nozawaholidays.com/holiday-nozawa-onsen-japan/snowfall-magic-on-mount-kenashi/","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"How do I get to Nozawa Onsen?","a":"**The terrain in numbers:** the resort rises from a **565 m** base to the **1,650 m** summit of Mt Kenashi — a **1,085 m vertical drop** — over **44.5 km of pistes** (22.1 km easy / 13 km intermediate / 9.4 km difficult) served by **16 lifts** including 2 gondolas (skiresort.info; consumer sources cite more).","source":"https://www.skiresort.info/ski-resort/nozawa-onsen/","accessed":"2026-07-18"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Nozawa Onsen?","a":"**A guided tree-riding day with Japan Snow Adventures** — expert-led powder tree lines through Kenashi''s forest with an operator that reads the conditions and carries rescue gear — Nozawa''s signature terrain, done safely — TIMING: Deep winter — **PRICE TIER `[premier]`** — COMMISSION: operator 10-15%","source":"https://japansnowadventures.com/","accessed":"2026-07-18"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Nozawa Onsen Guide: Onsen-Village Powder & the Fire Festival","meta_description":"Plan Nozawa Onsen, Japan - a 1,300-year onsen village and ski resort on Mt Kenashi: 1,085 m of deep powder, 13 free public hot springs, boutique ryokan and Japan''s Jan 15 Dosojin Fire Festival, two hours from Tokyo, with real timing, safety and booking intel.","slug":"nozawa-onsen-japan","primary_keyword":"Nozawa Onsen guide","long_tail":["Nozawa Onsen ski resort","Nozawa Onsen fire festival January 15","Nozawa Onsen free public baths soto-yu","how to get to Nozawa Onsen from Tokyo","Nozawa Onsen luxury ryokan chalet","Nozawa Onsen powder tree skiing"],"search_language":"ja","local_keywords":["野沢温泉スキー場","野沢温泉 道祖神祭り","野沢温泉 外湯","野沢温泉 大湯","野沢温泉 旅館","野沢菜"],"hreflang":["e