  ('machu-picchu-peru', '10S', 'Machu Picchu', 'Peru', 'A lost city in the clouds', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Cusco, Sacred Valley & Machu Picchu', '{"culture","expedition","rail","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Machu Picchu citadel sits at 2,430 m; Cusco gateway at ~3,400 m — altitude, not crime, is the headline planning constraint.","Entry is by timed circuit ticket only (no free roaming); daily cap 4,500 standard / 5,600 high season (Jun 19–Nov 2).","Classic Inca Trail is guided-mandatory, capped at 500 permits/day (~200 hikers), sells out 4–7 months ahead, and closes every February.","Cusco / Sacred Valley / Inca Trail / Machu Picchu are State-Dept-named as NOT in any higher-risk advisory area — the strongest clean-zone in South America.","Rail from Ollantaytambo (~1h45m) via PeruRail/Inca Rail; the Belmond Hiram Bingham is the luxury tier and bundles citadel entry, bus and guide."],"safety":{"emergency":"105","emergency_ambulance":"117","tourist_line":"iPerú / Policía de Turismo","hospital":"Cusco private clinics for routine + altitude care; serious cases evac to Lima (Clínica Anglo Americana / Ricardo Palma); Aguas Calientes + trail remote","air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Cusco (CUZ) via Lima (LIM); then rail Ollantaytambo → Aguas Calientes; shuttle bus to the gate","altitude_m":{"cusco":3400,"citadel":2430,"sacred_valley_base":2800,"dead_womans_pass":4215,"salkantay_pass":4650,"rainbow_mountain":5000},"altitude_note":"Acute mountain sickness (soroche) is the primary health risk; acclimatize in the lower Sacred Valley first, ascend gradually, coca tea","water":"bottled/purified only","malaria":"none at altitude (Cusco/Sacred Valley/Machu Picchu); malaria risk is in the low-elevation Amazon","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-09-01T16:20:02Z","page_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00","so