 the color bands past the pirate channel ·","commission":"affiliate ~4-8% (Viator/GYG) or lodge direct","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","tropical":"primary","wellness":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["affiliate","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Cenote Azul open-air swim","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable_category":"cenote entry","source":"https://kendyltravels.com/bacalar-cenotes/","hook":"~70 m-wide, ~90 m-deep sky cenote with rim restaurant ·","si":"tropical","blurb":"~70 m-wide, ~90 m-deep sky cenote with rim restaurant ·","commission":"non-commissionable gate; bundle into day-tour","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","tropical":"primary","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Cenote Negro (seventh color)","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"lagoon tour","source":"https://kendyltravels.com/bacalar-cenotes/","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-blue cenote said to complete the seven colors ·","si":"tropical","blurb":"the deep-blue cenote said to complete the seven colors ·","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate via tour","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","tropical":"primary","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Stromatolite kayak (Cenote Cocalitos)","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided eco-tour","source":"https://sandinmycurls.com/bacalar-mexico-seven-color-lagoon-guide/","si":"adventure","commission":"guided-tour affiliate; no-touch/no-sunscreen mandatory","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","tropical":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Eco-luxury lagoon lodge (Habitas / Boca de Agua)","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable_category":"boutique lodging","source":"https://www.bocadeagua.com/blog/best-hotels-bacalar-mexico","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"thatched cabins, yoga, clear kayaks, lagoon-front restaurant ·","si":"wellness","blurb":"thatched cabins, yoga, clear kayaks, lagoon-front restaurant ·","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"on application, 10%+ boutique/luxury","wells":["stay","eat","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["tropical","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","tropical":"evidenced","wellness":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band"},{"name":"Sunrise kayak + slow-water day","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"lodge activity","source":"https://www.bocadeagua.com/","si":"wellness","commission":"bundled in lodge rate","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","tropical":"destination","wellness":"primary"},"commission_lane":["bundle","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bacalar?","a":"Open-water swimming discipline, mosquitoes and hurricanes - not crime. Cenote Azul is a sky-facing sinkhole up to ~90m deep with no floor, so treat it as open water (strong swimmers/life vests); use repellent for dengue (present, worse in the rainy season); hurricane season runs Jun-Nov, peaking Aug-Oct.","source":"kendyltravels.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is the Lagoon of Seven Colors, and how do you see it?","a":"It''s a karst-fed freshwater lagoon whose colors shift from turquoise to navy over its sand, cenotes and varying depths. The signature way to see it is a half-day catamaran or sailboat circuit past Los Rapidos, the stromatolites and the Canal de los Piratas; go on a calm morning when the water is glass-still.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which are the best eco-luxury places to stay in Bacalar?","a":"Boca de Agua and Our Habitas Bacalar lead the lagoon. Boca de Agua is a Frida Escobedo-designed set of ~26 stilted treehouse villas on 82 acres with a MICHELIN Key 2025; Our Habitas is the established adults-only, wellness-led lagoon retreat ~20 min south of town. Both are direct/consortia bookings - book waterfront stock early for Dec-Apr.","source":"mrandmrssmith.com","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Bacalar?","a":"November-April, the dry season, is best - warm, mostly dry, with glass-still calm-water mornings. Within that, November and Feb-March are the best value (avoid Semana Santa); the rainy green season, Jun-Sep, is lush, quiet and cheapest but brings afternoon showers and hurricane overlap.","source":"hellobacalar.com","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bacalar Mexico: Lagoon of Seven Colors & Stromatolites","meta_description":"Bacalar''s Lagoon of Seven Colors, living stromatolites and open-air cenotes - where to sail, swim and stay, and how to protect what you came to see.","slug":"bacalar-mexico","primary_keyword":"Bacalar Lagoon of Seven Colors","long_tail":["Bacalar stromatolites","Cenote Azul Bacalar","Bacalar eco lodges","Bacalar sailboat tour","Bacalar things to do"],"search_language":"bilingual (en + es-MX)","local_keywords":["Laguna de los Siete Colores","Bacalar que hacer","estromatolitos Bacalar","Cenote Azul Ba