orts no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Whitewater rafting — Río Pastaza (Class III-IV)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-tours/White-Water-Rafting/d22150-g17-c27534","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local operator + activity affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Mirador Bellavista","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.ecuatouring.com/banos-travel-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","si":"expedition","blurb":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","when":"year-round","commission":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","romance":"evidenced","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Termas de la Virgen thermal baths (at night)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g312857-d20120113-Reviews-Termas_de_la_Virgen-Banos_Tungurahua_Province.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","si":"romance","blurb":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","when":"year-round","commission":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on","wells":["stay","beauty"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"primary","wellness":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Luna Volcán / former Luna Runtún — spa with volcano view","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/ec/luna-volcan-adventure-spa.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","si":"romance","blurb":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"primary","wellness":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort (converted monastery)","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/ecuador/samari.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","wellness":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the \"Swing at the End of the World\" worth it — and how much?","a":"Yes, and it is cheap — it is the image that put Baños on a million screens. The Casa del Árbol treehouse swing launches you out over the Tungurahua gorge from the Runtún ridge at ~2,600 m; the complex opens 07:00–19:00, entry is ~$1, and staff clip you into a climbing harness on a steel-beam frame.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Where can couples soak in thermal baths at night in Baños?","a":"At the Termas de la Virgen, in the town center beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall. Its sulfate-rich pools are heated by Tungurahua, open 05:00–17:00 and again 18:00–22:00, at ~$4 adult entry — the signature romantic-and-restorative Baños ritual, best paired with a volcano-view spa-hotel room-night.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Is Baños a genuine wellness and spa destination?","a":"Increasingly, yes — the town''s name literally means \"Baths of Holy Water.\" The anchor is Samari Spa Resort, a 300-year-old former Jesuit monastery on ~10 acres with a heated indoor pool, sauna, Turkish bath, whirlpool and full spa, ranked among Baños''s top hotels — mineral-rich thermal springs fed by Tungurahua''s volcanic heat make Baños a natural wellness base.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness-—-future-si","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Baños?","a":"Not urban crime — the load-bearing risk is activity risk. ~88% of Ecuador''s homicides occur in five coastal provinces, and the Andean highlands including Baños run below the homicide rates of many mid-sized US cities; the town''s core product is adrenaline (canyoning, Class III–IV rafting, the swing, highway cycling), so guided-vs-unguided is the whole game.","source":"myecuadorvisa.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Is the Tungurahua volcano dangerous right now?","a":"It is a real, live geohazard held quiet by monitoring — not a decorative caveat. Tungurahua erupted near-continuously 1999–2016, then went quiet; as of mid-2026 IG-EPN reports background/very-low activity with no precursor signals and 24/7 instrument monitoring, so any escalation would trigger alerts well in advance. Re-verify live IG-EPN status before booking.","source":"igepn.edu.ec, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"Is canyoning or the swing in Baños dangerous?","a":"Both carry real, activity-specific risk that guiding and gear mitigate. Canyoning on the Río Blanco is a guided-only roped waterfall-descent sport (helmet, harness, wetsuit, certified guide); the Casa del Árbol swing is 18+ with a ~220 lb (100 kg) weight limit and requires the operator''s climbing harness every ride. Never freelance either — book reputable operators like Geotours or Ivagatours.","source":"geotoursbanios.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador — The Swing, Waterfalls, Rafting & Thermal Baths | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Baños Ecuador","Casa del Árbol columpio","columpio fin del mundo Baños","Pailón del Diablo","Ruta de las Cascadas","rafting río Pastaza Baños","canyoning Baños","Termas de la Virgen","volcán Tungurahua estado","hoteles con spa en Baños"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Baños de Agua Santa","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:32Z","source_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Luna Volcán, Adventure SPA (formerly Luna Runtún)","category":"Boutique adventure-spa on Tungurahua''s flank, 30 rooms, 35-ha forest","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; Fora/host-agency on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort","category":"300-yr converted-monastery spa resort, ~10 acres","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; host-agency/Fora on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Casa del Suizo","category":"Amazon-edge Napo River jungle lodge (Ahuano), 75 rooms","mor":"DMC package / luxury-specialist — the Amazon-extend upsell","tier":"$$$-$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-1.3928,"lng":-78.4269},"orbit":[{"id":"cuenca-ecuador","jewels":10,"si":["culture"]},{"id":"galapagos-islands-ecuador","jewels":12,"si":["liveaboard","expedition"]},{"id":"quito-ecuador","jewels":11,"si":["culture"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 9),
  ('blue-hole-belize', '10S', 'The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole', 'Belize', 'Atolls, walls and the Blue Hole', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Belize', '{"liveaboard","expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Great Blue Hole is 318 m (1,043 ft) across and 124 m (407 ft) deep, near the center of Lighthouse Reef ~70 km (43 mi) off Belize City.","Belize has three coral atolls — Turneffe, Lighthouse Reef, Glover''s Reef — within the UNESCO-listed Belize Barrier Reef Reserve System.","Blue Hole stalactites hang at ~100-140 ft (30-42 m); the dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft with a narrow no-deco window — Advanced cert recommended.","Belize Aggressor III/IV depart Belize City Saturdays, up to 5 dives/day, 24-27 dives on a 7-night charter (39-42 on 10-night).","Whale sharks gather at Gladden Spit (southern Belize) around the full moon March-June."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Belize Chamber Project Ltd, San Pedro (Ambergris Caye) — only DAN-Preferred chamber in Belize, 24/7; hours of boat+air transit from the offshore atolls","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco dive / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before BZE flight home","water":"open Caribbean ocean; no malaria offshore; high sun/sea exposure; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","read":"2026-09-01T16:20:07Z","page_updated":"2026-06-12T10:40:30+01:00","source_country":"belize","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar","dive_calendar":true,"curve_start":"2026-02-15","peak":"March-June (Blue Hole best flat seas April-June)","whale_shark_window":["2026-03-14","2026-04-13","2026-05-12","2026-06-11"],"booking_lead_months":"4-6 (peak charters / full-boat buyouts longer)","shoulder_green_season":"September-November (wet/rougher, off-season fill)","fire_date":"2026-02-01","trigger_date":"2026-02-01","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor charter availability + whale-shark sighting logs; flat-sea onset shifts yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Great Blue Hole (Lighthouse Reef)","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Blue_Hole","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Aggressor)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["diveglobal","expedition","liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed","si_raw":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Dive Liveaboards/GEA'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Half Moon Caye Wall + Natural Monument","tier":"premier","source":"https://ambergriscaye.com/pages/town/divelighthouse.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","when":"year-round","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane; park fee non-commissionable","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed","si_raw":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"The Painted Wall & Quebrada (Lighthouse Reef)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/Belize","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Turneffe Elbow (Turneffe Atoll)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.divessi.com/en/mydiveguide/divesite/98293","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or Fora via Turneffe resorts","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["diveglobal","expedition","liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Dive Liveaboards/GEA'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Glover''s Reef (remote atoll)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane (scarcity — few boats reach it)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["diveglobal","expedition","liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed","si_raw":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Dive Liveaboards/GEA'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Gladden Spit whale sharks (seasonal, southern Belize)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://belizescuba.com/diving-snorkeling/whale-sharks/","si":"liveaboard","commission":"AFF/day-operator or Fora via Placencia; marine-reserve fee non-commissionable","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["diveglobal","expedition","liveaboard"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"evidenced","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''GEA/Dive Liveaboards'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Tobacco Caye","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora lane (small guesthouse packages)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":["package"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Long Caye (Lighthouse Reef)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizehighcommission.com/areas-of-belize/lighthouse-reef-bz","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on operator","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["diveglobal","liveaboard","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"destination","liveaboard":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"How many dives do you get on a Belize Aggressor liveaboard trip?","a":"Up to five dives a day — 24–27 dives on a 7-night charter, 39–42 on a 10-night. The Aggressor III/IV depart the Fort George dock in Belize City every Saturday at 6 pm, dive Sunday morning to Friday noon, and reach all three atolls, so the liveaboard converts a long day-boat run into unlimited access to Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe and Glover''s.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"How deep is the Great Blue Hole dive and do you need to be certified?","a":"The dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft — at or beyond the recreational limit — to see the stalactites that hang between roughly 100–140 ft. Bottom time is measured in minutes and nitrogen narcosis is a real factor, so reputable operators strongly recommend or require Advanced Open Water certification. It is a deliberately deep dive, not a beginner novelty.","source":"dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"What is there to do on the Belize atolls if you don''t dive?","a":"The atoll cayes carry barefoot reef-island character for surface-interval and non-diver days. Tobacco Caye is a few-acre reef caye with snorkel-off-the-dock access; Half Moon Caye is a natural monument with ~4,000 nesting red-footed boobies and an observation tower; Long Caye is the inhabited base camp for Blue Hole and Half Moon Caye dives.","source":"belizeadventure.ca, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on an atoll dive trip?","a":"Offshore remoteness from the chamber. The only DAN-Preferred recompression chamber in Belize is on San Pedro, Ambergris Caye — hours of boat-then-air transit from a hit at Lighthouse Reef (~70 km/43 mi offshore) or Glover''s. Liveaboards carry onboard O2 and run DAN protocols as first response, which is why depth and deco discipline are non-negotiable and DAN insurance with evacuation coverage is effectively mandatory.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"How long do you have to wait to fly after diving the Blue Hole?","a":"Plan an 18–24 hour buffer. DAN guidance sets a minimum 12-hour surface interval after a single no-deco dive and a minimum 18 hours after multi-day repetitive diving, which every liveaboard trip is; 24 hours is the recommended general practice. A 7-night Aggressor charter ends diving Friday around noon for a Saturday departure precisely to give that buffer before the BZE flight home.","source":"dan.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Blue Hole & Belize Atolls Diving — Liveaboard, Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe & Glover''s | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Belize Blue Hole liveaboard","diving Lighthouse Reef Belize","Belize Aggressor","Great Blue Hole dive depth","Turneffe Atoll diving","Glover''s Reef liveaboard","Half Moon Caye Wall dive","Belize whale shark diving Gladden Spit","no fly after diving Belize"],"hreflang":["en"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:57Z","source_updated":"2026-06-12T10:40:30+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat liveaboard charter (Belize Aggressor III/IV buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/belize"},{"name":"Turneffe Island Resort (luxury all-inclusive dive)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA) all-inclusive dive package","source":"https://visitturneffe.org/discover/where-to-stay-on-turneffe-atoll/"},{"name":"Gladden Private Island (adjacent, southern Belize)","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on channel","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.3158,"lng":-87.5346},"orbit":[{"id":"ambergris-caye-belize","jewels":11,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","romance","expedition"]},{"id":"caye-caulker-belize","jewels":9,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","expedition","ocean","culinary"]},{"id":"hopkins-belize","jewels":8,"si":["tropical","expedition","culture"]},{"id":"placencia-belize","jewels":8,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","diveglobal","ocean","wildlife","culture"]},{"id":"san-ignacio-belize","jewels":13,"si":["expedition","culture","romance"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 10),
